#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
@ — a tiny shell-native wrapper around AI coding agents (Codex, Claude Code, opencode, Gemini).

Usage:
  @ fix the failing tests
  @ explain this stack trace
  @ --use claude
  @ --new
  @ --status
  @ --forget

Behavior:
  - One persistent conversation per backend per git repository (or current directory).
  - Backend is chosen per project: @ --use codex|claude|opencode|gemini
  - Commands are always '--' prefixed; everything else is a prompt.
  - Piped stdin becomes labeled context:  git diff | @ "review this"
  - Normal shell commands remain normal shell commands.
  - State is stored in:
      ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/at-agent/
"""

